# Vitest always writes snapshot files with LF. Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true,
# the default) checks every text file out as CRLF, so the first test run after a
# checkout, pull or new worktree rewrote each *.snap as LF and `git status` then
# showed them as modified with no real change. Checking snapshots out as LF in the
# first place means a run never has anything to rewrite.
#
# Scoped to snapshots on purpose: it does not renormalize the rest of the repo.
*.snap text eol=lf
